1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Welcome to the Dark Malta Festival!

2
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
I'm back on Malta for the Dark Malta Festival because I just love the weather here, the location, the bands, the festival.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,200
It is awesome. So let's come along and join me to interview some bands to dance a lot and just have a great time

4
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:32,500
for my Malta holiday

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,000
2026 let's go

6
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:05,200
So with me is Alex from Den Con Silence.

7
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:07,000
I just saw you on stage.

8
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,160
How was the gig?

9
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:13,200
It was fun and it was a great crowd and a very cool festival.

10
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:15,840
Because we heard of this place, never been here before.

11
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:21,120
Tiny island, you can drive from one point to the other end of the island in like 20

12
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:22,120
minutes.

13
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:24,120
and it's really hard to find on the map.

14
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:25,120
Like, where is Malta?

15
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:29,120
You have to try to zoom out and like, oh, there it is.

16
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:31,120
So yeah, but it's cute.

17
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:34,120
I've seen you on your tour, on festivals.

18
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:40,120
What is the difference between a festival setup and a tour setlist?

19
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:43,120
At the moment, I actually prefer festivals

20
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:47,120
because I can put more energy into one spot.

21
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:51,120
You know, like, let's do this show and put 100%.

22
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:59,680
Tour is exhausting because some days you wake up, maybe you're sore in your throat or you can be hangover.

23
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:07,080
It can be ups and downs, but festivals, I actually prefer festivals. I have more fun.

24
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,340
Alright, thank you so much.

25
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:08,980
See you then.

26
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:24,120
I'm a god of emotions

27
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:27,120
Now she knows what I feel

28
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:30,120
But she didn't say a word

29
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:33,120
Stood bare with a heart of steel

30
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:36,120
She doesn't know how much it hurts

31
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:39,120
Again my eyes run dry

32
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:43,120
Into the ocean I cry

33
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:46,120
Okay, two minutes before the show with exercise.

34
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:48,120
Let's do the pre-show preparations.

35
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:54,680
Yes. First, knees. Grab it. Not at the foot, but at the ankle.

36
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:56,840
Yes, yeah. Left. Other one. Yes.

37
00:02:58,840 --> 00:03:05,320
Okay. Now stretch your back. Knee stays. Okay. Touch the ground. Yes, I touch the ground.

38
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:15,320
And now left. Okay. And right. Right. Other side. Other side. Ah!

39
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:19,720
Okay, and very important to play the call-bell.

40
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:20,720
Here.

41
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:26,720
Because for the perfect call-bell song you have to break your ankle.

42
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:27,720
Break your ankle?

43
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:28,720
Break your ankle.

44
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:29,720
Doesn't sound healthy.

45
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:30,720
Yeah, it's not healthy.

46
00:03:30,720 --> 00:03:31,720
It's a call-bell.

47
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:33,720
Alright.

48
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:34,720
That's the pre-show routine.

49
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:35,720
Alright, let's go.

50
00:03:35,720 --> 00:04:05,700
We'll be right back.

51
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:16,480
So I'm here with Das Ich.

52
00:04:16,980 --> 00:04:17,280
Yes.

53
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:18,100
Yes.

54
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:19,300
And you're at Malta.

55
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:20,180
At Malta.

56
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:21,980
Stefan and Sven.

57
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:22,580
And me.

58
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:26,240
You're three persons and call yourself Das Ich, which is one person.

59
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:29,380
No, well, the ego is having three parts.

60
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:32,300
Now you can guess who is who.

61
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:36,300
You're from Germany, as I am.

62
00:04:36,300 --> 00:04:39,460
How did it come that you're playing at Malta?

63
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:40,460
That's a good question.

64
00:04:40,460 --> 00:04:45,640
It's also for us the first time at Malta at the Dark Malta Festival and we just got the

65
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:51,640
invitation a year ago so we had been really happy and of course it's a bit like a vacation

66
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:58,360
so we came already on Friday and we're enjoying two days of beach so it was really awesome.

67
00:04:58,360 --> 00:04:59,360
Beach!

68
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:01,540
What did you do at a beach at Goth People?

69
00:05:01,540 --> 00:05:04,540
We are humans.

70
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:06,540
Yeah, we like beach.

71
00:05:06,540 --> 00:05:08,540
Did you use 50 plus sunscreen?

72
00:05:08,540 --> 00:05:10,540
Of course.

73
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:15,540
No, but actually I love this kind of weather, especially after winter time.

74
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:20,540
I mean, it's warm, but it's not so warm because it's quite windy.

75
00:05:20,540 --> 00:05:23,540
So it's perfect for the goth people, not too hot.

76
00:05:23,540 --> 00:05:26,540
You've been in the business a long time.

77
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:33,540
We've seen so many festivals like the old festivals in Germany, Mera Luna, Amphi, WGT, everything.

78
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:38,540
How is it to play at a relatively new festival where you've never been before?

79
00:05:38,540 --> 00:05:44,540
Well, there's always popping and especially in the last years there were popping up a lot of new festivals.

80
00:05:44,540 --> 00:05:50,540
And honestly, I'm always really happy because new festival also means new kind of crowd sometimes.

81
00:05:50,540 --> 00:05:57,540
Of course here it is more like I would say people what you also see at the Amphi festival or so.

82
00:05:57,540 --> 00:05:58,540
I saw a lot of Amphi t-shirts.

83
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:02,540
Yes, definitely. Therefore I refer on that.

84
00:06:02,540 --> 00:06:10,540
But basically we love the small new festivals. There's a few in Germany and in other regions.

85
00:06:10,540 --> 00:06:15,540
We're going now for a tour in the United States, also playing there some festival.

86
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:19,740
and it's always beautiful because you can reach out to new people,

87
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:22,460
sometimes young people who never have heard of you,

88
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:24,720
especially when you're so old like us.

89
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:26,540
But yeah, you're true.

90
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:31,740
We even remember the days really quite vividly

91
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:34,860
when Mira Luna was still called Cello Festival,

92
00:06:35,220 --> 00:06:37,340
so we played like the first Cello Festival.

93
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:40,560
What is your plan for the future of the band,

94
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:43,840
being said that you're in a business for so many years already?

95
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:44,900
Staying alive!

96
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:46,220
going till die.

97
00:06:47,220 --> 00:06:48,580
Till you die. Of course.

98
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:50,620
It's my dream

99
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:52,480
to just light up

100
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:54,720
on this cross when I'm hanging

101
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:56,260
on the singing goddess' throne.

102
00:06:56,420 --> 00:06:57,220
Just in the moment,

103
00:06:58,020 --> 00:06:59,560
burn, baby, burn.

104
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:02,360
And you must know, it's really a privilege.

105
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:04,760
I just was thinking about that

106
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:06,400
the last days. I mean,

107
00:07:06,540 --> 00:07:08,380
this is really a beautiful holiday

108
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:10,920
location where people pay lots of money

109
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:12,560
to fly here, to have

110
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:13,760
hotel and so on.

111
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:20,300
And we are having this privileged life to just hang out here, getting even paid for doing this.

112
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:23,880
So there is nothing you can ever complain about.

113
00:07:24,060 --> 00:07:26,220
Therefore, of course, we try to go on.

114
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:34,900
And we're really thankful that there is not only so many old followers who are fully supporting us by buying our records and merchandise.

115
00:07:35,060 --> 00:07:36,480
It's also many young people.

116
00:07:37,100 --> 00:07:40,840
And it was for us really beautiful with the last new album, Fanal.

117
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:45,880
because we suddenly we were first a bit afraid like how will be the response but

118
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:51,340
it was so awesome response and that was going so well so this gave us a lot of

119
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:55,600
motivation to go on and we're actually already again working on new tracks

120
00:07:55,600 --> 00:08:01,020
mostly was very afraid because it took so long time and maybe the people forgot

121
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:08,500
us I wish you a lot of fun at the gig tonight and thank you thank you very

122
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:11,500
Thank you very much and support this great channel!

123
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:11,500
Attention! Attention! I'm coming!

124
00:09:38,500 --> 00:09:41,960
You did some sightseeing already. What can you recommend to do on Malta?

125
00:09:43,260 --> 00:09:50,360
First, the island Goso is awesome. There's an old ancient ruin. This was awesome for me and Valetta at night

126
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:57,140
Beautiful. I mean according to a song the sea I would say the sea

127
00:09:58,160 --> 00:10:04,720
Yeah, it's a little bit cold, but it works. The sea in April is quite cold on Malta. I've been there

128
00:10:04,720 --> 00:10:08,060
I was like nope, nope, nope. Beautiful country

129
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:15,120
I mean you've already played on several German festivals, like old school festivals. How was it to be a malta? Was there a difference?

130
00:10:17,380 --> 00:10:23,780
I mean, I would say the biggest difference was playing an acoustic drum kit today, first time for Elionair.

131
00:10:24,880 --> 00:10:26,880
Usually we play e-drums.

132
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:31,260
But I quite liked it. Yeah, it was great.

133
00:10:31,820 --> 00:10:37,220
Especially because no one of us had his own instrument, so it was like a little surprise.

134
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:39,220
You borrowed the instruments?

135
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:42,220
Yeah, we borrowed the instruments so we came on stage and it was like,

136
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:44,220
oh let's see which keyboard do you have?

137
00:10:44,220 --> 00:10:46,220
And this one was great!

138
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:50,220
And the same was with the drum set because, as you said, normally we play E-drums

139
00:10:50,220 --> 00:10:53,220
and today it was acoustic but it sounded really great.

140
00:10:53,220 --> 00:10:57,220
Great team here, great get-rigged-sound guy, everything perfect.

141
00:10:57,220 --> 00:10:59,220
So, yeah, they made it easy for us.

142
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:04,220
So, did you play better without your original instruments?

143
00:11:04,220 --> 00:11:06,500
I wouldn't say that.

144
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:11,040
Because normally we got a sound directly in the ears

145
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:12,820
and today we had a monitor sound.

146
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:15,080
So it was a bit strange.

147
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:16,580
Old school monitor sound.

148
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:17,900
It was a little bit difficult.

149
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:19,400
So I would say no.

150
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:24,520
But it was for not playing your own instrument, it was good.

151
00:11:24,860 --> 00:11:26,480
The crowd was very international.

152
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:31,220
They are also shearing up and waving their hands like in our normal shows.

153
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:32,140
It was awesome.

154
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:33,200
The crowd here is awesome.

155
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:33,980
Yeah, definitely.

156
00:11:33,980 --> 00:11:35,320
They're really, really nice, really friendly.

157
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:35,960
Yeah.

158
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:37,860
So happy you enjoyed it.

159
00:11:38,620 --> 00:11:40,700
Hopefully we will be here one day again.

160
00:11:40,900 --> 00:11:42,560
Well, you have to tell it to Rene, not me.

161
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:43,080
Okay.

162
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:45,100
But maybe he will see it.

163
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:01,820
I cried an ocean of fear

164
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:05,020
Because it gets worse and worse

165
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:07,840
Went through rivers of tears

166
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:10,760
And no one sees how much it hurts

167
00:12:10,760 --> 00:12:12,920
All right, Rene, here we are again,

168
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,460
organizer of Dark Malta Festival.

169
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:16,740
We've seen each other like three years ago.

170
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:18,400
Three years ago, I think it was the last time, yeah.

171
00:12:18,680 --> 00:12:20,540
How did the festival develop?

172
00:12:21,100 --> 00:12:23,920
What would you say is the resume of the three years?

173
00:12:23,940 --> 00:12:25,680
After three years, it developed very well now.

174
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:27,820
I mean, the crowd is increasing year by year.

175
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:30,040
Even the venue, we're trying to give it more,

176
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:30,860
a bigger look now.

177
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:40,160
I mean, we've changed the system of the entrance, bigger food court, the pool party is now it's like an establishment, you know, it's like year by year they're getting bigger.

178
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:45,740
We've increased also to other days because we're doing the pre-party on Thursday and also a boat party on Monday.

179
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:51,700
So it's like now it's a five day festival, it's not anymore a three day festival and people are coming from all over the world.

180
00:12:52,060 --> 00:12:52,800
Yes, nice.

181
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:57,580
I noticed that the pool party is way bigger and that there are more people overall here.

182
00:12:57,860 --> 00:12:58,260
That's right.

183
00:12:58,260 --> 00:13:01,260
Yes. So what are your plans for the future?

184
00:13:01,820 --> 00:13:03,620
There are some nice plans for the future.

185
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:06,920
I cannot until now announce anything.

186
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:11,320
The venue is already giving a hint what's going to be the future of Dark Malta.

187
00:13:11,940 --> 00:13:15,560
So yes, we've got bigger plans coming in,

188
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:17,420
maybe also from next year for Dark Malta.

189
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:22,840
We're in the process of announcing some big headliners by the end of April,

190
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:25,180
so we're really looking forward for next year already.

191
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:28,840
because actually the work for next year started from last January.

192
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:33,420
I've talked to so many bands already and they all said it's so special to be here on Malta.

193
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:38,340
So why should bands come here and apply to play at the festival? What would you say?

194
00:13:39,060 --> 00:13:43,720
I believe it's a different market. I mean, it's not like the other European festivals

195
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:46,700
because even the location by itself, it's a very exotic location.

196
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:51,460
The weather, you know, the country itself. I mean, it's April, it's already summer nearly.

197
00:13:51,460 --> 00:13:55,460
So I mean even the crowd the energy is different because I'm in the warm weather

198
00:13:56,180 --> 00:13:58,180
Everyone's relaxed everyone's

199
00:13:58,180 --> 00:14:01,540
Exactly, everybody, you know come first go to the beach then they will come to the party

200
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:05,380
So there's a special energy going on also. Our crew is very very good

201
00:14:05,380 --> 00:14:08,180
I mean it has been praised by all the bands after all their shows. So

202
00:14:08,980 --> 00:14:14,260
We're really looking forward to have more new bands playing at dark walter and there will be more new bands playing at dark walter

203
00:14:14,340 --> 00:14:20,260
So yes, so i'm so looking forward to the announcements until next year. Thanks so much. Thanks a lot. Thanks for coming again

204
00:14:21,460 --> 00:14:28,140
It's the last day of my Malta trip and I'm doing a very quick photoshoot here by the

205
00:14:28,140 --> 00:14:34,220
sea, but it's been another amazing trip here on this island and to dark Malta of course.

206
00:14:34,220 --> 00:14:37,560
I am so happy that I was able to come back.

207
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:38,560
Thanks for watching.

208
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:42,740
Quite a few people approached me during the festival and told me that they're basically

209
00:14:42,740 --> 00:14:48,260
here on the festival because they saw my YouTube videos in the previous years and that makes

210
00:14:48,260 --> 00:14:50,280
me so glad and so happy.

211
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:55,360
So thanks for watching and if you thought, well, that is a great festival, then maybe

212
00:14:55,360 --> 00:14:57,120
I'll see you next year.

213
00:14:57,120 --> 00:14:58,120
Have a nice day.

214
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:58,620
Bye.

